 "kind": "multimat",
 "brief": "I want a vibration-isolating mount for a small camera on my robot arm's base, printed in PETG\nand TPU 95A on a two-material FDM printer, flat on the bed (layers along Z, base down). The\nbottom is a PETG flange, z = 0 to 4, that screws down to the arm with four M3 screws along Z\nat (+-24, +-24): 3.4 mm holes, and the screw heads need 7 mm diameter clearance above the\nflange up to z = 20. The camera sits on a 32 x 32 mm PETG top plate,\nz = 9 to 13, centred over the origin, fixed with four M2.5 screws from above at (+-10, +-10)\ninto 2.2 mm pilot holes 4 mm deep from the top face. Between the flange and the top plate is a\n5 mm TPU layer (z = 4 to 9) under the whole top plate: the vibration must go through rubber,\nso there must be no PETG path at all from the flange to the top plate. Everything fits in\nx, y = -30 to 30, z = 0 to 13. Loads: the flange screws hold it; the camera is 150 g, and with\nthe arm's shocks design for 15 N pushing down on the top plate, and 10 N sideways along X on\nthe top plate. Safety factor 3 on the plastics and on the TPU-PETG bond, and under 25 g.",
 "attachments": [],
